  "rendered": {
    "title": "Fresh-chat routing, session hydration, and public chat polish",
    "intro": "Today's nightly centered on making chat routes durable across fresh sends, taskbar returns, and reloads, with a parallel pass of polish on the public chat experience and a small but important fix to how the macOS desktop window comes up on launch.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "3:10 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-06T10:10:14.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-06T11:12:59.000Z",
        "title": "Fresh chat canvases bind to real sessions after first send",
        "summary": "Reworked how the chat app treats a fresh canvas so the first send reliably materializes into a persisted session and the URL follows along.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Fixed the fresh-canvas state so any URL without a session id is treated as pending, and the fresh key is threaded through so a new send is correctly armed as a new session instead of getting bound to a stale one.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "378f600c5228f09599987bac03d044eb54172742"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "After the first send lands, the chat route now swaps the throwaway fresh=... param for a canonical project/instance/session/agent URL, and share links read from that canonical route so copied links point at the real session.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8a544bb1af43f8c12af172696475bc79ccf5f9ce",
              "164f2d284ed67ccf98905fb5d36ac7c73e4f767b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "4:46 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-06T11:46:11.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-06T12:06:07.000Z",
        "title": "macOS desktop window visible on launch",
        "summary": "The desktop app now shows its main window on launch on macOS, while keeping the headless behavior CI depends on.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "The macOS desktop build now presents the main window on launch instead of starting hidden, so first-run and relaunch actually surface the app.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "26652002eccb3224a38fc46f43e80fdb8ac07fd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "CI runs still launch the desktop hidden by detecting standard CI environment variables, so the visible-on-launch change doesn't destabilize automated desktop tests.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c9d2b5c3280f2d0dd169b255ef381836fbe8d8c0",
              "a3ca860b5a2cb427c1d20bcb6b4df8f8beb8b6d9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "5:47 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-06T12:47:35.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-06T15:19:13.000Z",
        "title": "Taskbar remembers your last chat, and web session lists stop breaking on bad data",
        "summary": "The chat taskbar entry now returns you to the exact session you were last in, session list hydration is hardened against malformed data, and the mobile public chat shell got a real touch-target and safe-area pass.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Clicking the chat app from the nav rail now restores the last concrete session route (project, instance, session, agent) instead of dropping you on a blank canvas, with legacy session-only links upgraded to share-capable URLs.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5f2505a149201c5c6445d84b738a7586f86b98ef"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Tightened the rule for remembering a route so no-agent session URLs are only persisted once the session's real owner has loaded, preventing a bad agent from being written into the remembered route.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "debe58e330f55ee702957f896b6a7e4eccf5ad92"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
